---
import Presentation from "../../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Spec = `PROGRAM: ..........................................

WHAT IT DOES, in two sentences:
  ..................................................
  ..................................................

WHO WOULD USE IT, and what they need from it:
  ..................................................

INPUT      what you ask for, and how ...............
LIST       its name, what is in it .................
           and why the program breaks without it ...
PROCEDURE  its name ................................
PARAMETER  and what changes when it changes ........
INSIDE IT  the loop ................................
           the decision ............................
OUTPUT     what comes out, and what it depends on ..`;

const TenLines = `Something WORKING at the end of every session.
Not "keep going" -- something you could show me.

  55  ............................................
  56  ............................................
  57  ............................................
  58  ............................................
  59  ............................................
  60  ............................................
  61  ............................................
  62  ............................................
  63  the Project Reference
  64  the video, and submit

FIRST THING I CUT if I run out of time:
  ..............................................`;

const IncrementalVsNot = `INCREMENTAL                    ALL AT ONCE

55  list + print it            55  write everything
56  the procedure, called      56  write everything
57  the loop inside it         57  write everything
58  the decision               58  write everything
59  input                      59  nothing runs yet
60  output tidy                60  still nothing runs
61  a second feature           61  panic
62  polish                     62  panic

Working at 8 checkpoints.       Working at 0.`;

const WrOneTest = `Say your program's purpose out loud in one sentence.

  Does it name a PERSON?           yes / no
  Does it name what they NEED?     yes / no

If either is no, you cannot answer Written Response 1,
and Written Response 1 is one of your six points.`;

const TestData = `Three inputs, written BEFORE you build:

  a normal one ........  input ______  expected ______
  the smallest one ....  input ______  expected ______
  one just past the
  edge ...............  input ______  expected ______

The last one is where programs break.
You have known this since session 10.`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Activity 3.2: The Create Task &mdash; The Proposal</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Brief -->
        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Last Day I Can Help</h2>

          <p>
            <b>No code today.</b> Today you write a specification and I approve it.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">This is the last session where I am allowed to
            tell you your plan is too big, your list is decoration, or your procedure
            has nothing in it.</b> From session 55 the answer to every question like
            that is that I cannot say.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>Use me.</b> Twenty minutes of me telling you something is wrong today
            is worth more than eight sessions of building the wrong thing.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>Activity 3.2</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">The Create Task &mdash; The Proposal</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Concepts</h2>
              <p>A Specification</p>
              <p>Incremental Development</p>
              <p>Deciding the Cut in Advance</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>What You Are Writing</h2>
              <p>A <b class="text-sn-theme">specification</b> &mdash; a written statement of what the program must do.</p>
              <p class="fragment">You have written two of these. The Build 1 and Build 2 gate sheets were specifications.</p>
              <p class="fragment">This is the same thing with its proper name on it.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Where a Specification Comes From</h2>
              <p><b>Investigation.</b> You find out what is needed before you decide what to build.</p>
              <p class="fragment">Surveys. Interviews. Watching someone try to do the thing.</p>
              <p class="fragment">You have ten minutes, not ten weeks &mdash; so ask <b>one person</b> what would be useful.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Why That Matters for Your Grade</h2>
              <p>Written Response 1: <i>name an expected user, and describe one way your design meets their needs.</i></p>
              <p class="fragment"><b>You cannot answer that in May if you never decided who it was for.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">One of your six points is decided today, not in the exam room.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Two Ways to Build Eight Sessions</h2>
              <Code code={IncrementalVsNot} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Incremental, or Not" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment">The left column is <b class="text-sn-theme">incremental development</b>.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Incremental</h2>
              <p><b>Break the problem into pieces. Make each piece work before adding the next.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">That is the definition, and it is on the exam.</p>
              <p class="fragment">It is also the only way to have something to submit if session 61 goes badly.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>And Iterative</h2>
              <p><b>Going back.</b> Revising an earlier decision because testing told you to.</p>
              <p class="fragment">Not a sign you planned badly.</p>
              <p class="fragment">
                The exam calls a development process <b>iterative</b> when it{" "}
                <i>requires refinement and revision based on feedback, testing, or
                reflection throughout</i>.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>So Your Ten Lines Will Be Wrong</h2>
              <p>They were wrong at Build 1. They were wrong at Build 2.</p>
              <p class="fragment"><b>Write them anyway.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">A plan you deviate from is navigation. No plan is drifting.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Name the Cut Now</h2>
              <p>What is the first thing to go if you run out of time?</p>
              <p class="fragment">Decide it today, while it costs nothing.</p>
              <p class="fragment">At session 61 you will not be making a good decision about this.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>The Journal</h2>
              <p><b>One line at the end of every session.</b> What you did, and what you were in the middle of.</p>
              <p class="fragment">It is worth <b>40 points</b>, graded on whether it is there.</p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Not on whether it is good &mdash; because judging whether it is good
                would be feedback, and I am not allowed to give you any.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>What the Journal Is Really For</h2>
              <p>Session 58 opens and you have forgotten everything.</p>
              <p class="fragment">Also: <b>it is where Written Response 1 comes from.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">Design decisions, written down while you remember why you made them.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>One More Thing to Write Today</h2>
              <p><b>Three test inputs</b>, and what each should produce.</p>
              <p class="fragment">A normal one. The smallest one. <b class="text-sn-theme">One just past the edge.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">You have been finding boundary bugs since session 10. Same skill, your own program.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Today's Objectives</h2>
              <ul>
                <li>Writing a specification that names a user and their need</li>
                <li>Planning eight sessions incrementally, with something working at each step</li>
                <li>Explaining the difference between an incremental and an iterative process</li>
                <li>Naming in advance what will be cut</li>
                <li>Identifying test inputs at and just beyond the extremes</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Terms</h2>
              <div class="text-start">
                <dl>
                  <dt>Specification</dt>
                  <dd>A statement of the requirements for a program.</dd>
                  <dt>Incremental development</dt>
                  <dd>Breaking a problem into smaller pieces and making each one work before adding it to the whole.</dd>
                  <dt>Iterative development</dt>
                  <dd>Refining and revising based on feedback, testing, or reflection &mdash; including revisiting earlier phases.</dd>
                  <dt>Investigation</dt>
                  <dd>Finding out a program's requirements before designing it &mdash; surveys, interviews, user testing, observation.</dd>
                </dl>
              </div>
            </section>
          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- The gate -->
        <section id="gate">
          <h2>The Gate</h2>

          <p>
            <b>Fill this in. Bring it to me. No code until it is initialed.</b>
          </p>

          <Code code={Spec} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Your Specification" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <h5 class="mt-4">Ten lines for ten sessions</h5>

          <Code code={TenLines} frame="code" lang="txt" title="The Plan" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-3">
            <b>Sessions 63 and 64 are already spent</b> &mdash; the Project Reference
            and the video. That leaves you <b>eight</b>. Plan eight, not ten.
          </p>

          <h5 class="mt-4">The seven checks</h5>

          <p>I will ask you these. About a minute each.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>Can you name the list, and say why the program breaks without it?</li>
            <li>Can you name the procedure and its parameter, and say what changes when the parameter changes?</li>
            <li>Is there a loop <b>and</b> a decision inside that procedure?</li>
            <li>Eight lines for eight sessions, each one something I could check?</li>
            <li>What will you cut first?</li>
            <li><b>Who is this for, and what do they need from it?</b></li>
            <li><b>Is this a new program?</b></li>
          </ol>

          <p class="mt-3">
            <b>Checks 6 and 7 are new.</b> Six is Written Response 1, decided in
            advance. <b>Seven is because you may not submit Build 2 or any part of
            it</b> &mdash; that is a College Board rule about practice performance
            tasks, and it is not negotiable.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Today's Work</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 1: Ask One Person</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Describe your idea to someone in the room in two sentences.</li>
            <li>Ask them: <b>what would make this actually useful to you?</b></li>
            <li>Write down what they said, even if you disagree with it.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            <b>That is investigation, and it takes three minutes.</b> The exam calls
            surveys, interviews, user testing and direct observation the ways to do
            it. You just did the second one.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 2: The Purpose Test</h3>
          <Code code={WrOneTest} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Can You Answer WR1?" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-3">
            <b>&quot;A game&quot; fails this test. &quot;Anyone&quot; fails this
            test.</b> Fix the sentence until it names somebody and something they
            need.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 3: The Specification and the Plan</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Fill in both sheets above.</li>
            <li>Bring them to me for approval.</li>
            <li><b>Then start building.</b> Session 55 is not the start &mdash; today is, once you are approved.</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 4: Three Test Inputs</h3>
          <Code code={TestData} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Before You Build" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-3">
            <b>Writing these before the code is the point.</b> Test data invented
            afterward tends to be data the program already handles.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>
            <b>An initialed specification, an eight-line plan, a named first cut, and
            three test inputs.</b>
          </p>

          <p>
            If you are not approved by the end of this session, you start session 55
            without a plan &mdash; and session 55 is the first day I cannot help you
            make one. <b class="text-sn-theme">Do not leave here unapproved.</b>
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer these before submitting your work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>What did the person you asked in Task 1 say, and did it change your plan? &quot;No&quot; is a fine answer if you say why.</li>
            <li>Your Build 2 plan was wrong somewhere. Which line of it went wrong, and what did you do about it at the time?</li>
            <li>Explain the difference between an <b>incremental</b> and an <b>iterative</b> development process, in your own words, using your own plan as the example.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your initialed specification, your eight-line plan, your three test
            inputs, and your reflection.
          </p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Activity Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
